---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const ms = [
  ['Foundations', 'Done', 'Workspace, CI, licences, contributing guide, privacy policy.'],
  ['Daemon and window', 'In progress', 'Resident daemon with a pre-built GTK window, hotkeys, apps, ranking. Open latency still to be measured.'],
  ['Answers engine', 'Written, being polished', 'Maths, units, currency, time, emoji and colours, with golden tests.'],
  ['Files, folders, search, shell', 'Planned', 'File indexer, quick folders, web search on request, shell commands.'],
  ['System and windows', 'Planned', 'Lock, sleep, restart, kill and kill port, settings panels, window switching on X11, KDE, Hyprland, Sway, GNOME and macOS.'],
  ['Settings and plugins', 'Planned', 'Settings app, styles, plugin host, example plugins, signed registry.'],
  ['Packaging and 1.0', 'Planned', 'Packages, measured performance numbers, the 1.0 release.'],
];
const post = [
  ['Clipboard history', 'Encrypted, with a skip list for password managers.'],
  ['Snippets', 'Short triggers with date and cursor placeholders.'],
  ['Connectors', 'Quick commands for music players, notes and editors.'],
  ['Plugin browser', 'Install community plugins from inside the app.'],
];
---
<Base title="Roadmap: Fudge" description="Milestones for Fudge, from workspace to 1.0, and what comes after.">
  <article class="page">
    <h1>Roadmap</h1>
    <p class="lead">The plan, not a promise of dates. Status labels may lag the repository.</p>
    <h2>Toward 1.0</h2>
    <ol class="steps">
      {ms.map(([t, s, d]) => (<li><h3>{t}</h3><p class="state">{s}</p><p>{d}</p></li>))}
    </ol>
    <h2>After 1.0</h2>
    <ul class="steps">
      {post.map(([t, d]) => (<li><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p></li>))}
    </ul>
    <h2>Targets</h2>
    <p>Open in about 10 ms and use about 50 MB of memory. These are goals, not measurements. Numbers will be published with 1.0.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
